WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.550
Verse 4

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.550
Nobody 
wishes
to see

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:21.970
Yoshino
 Tournament

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:21.970
Quarterfinals

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.270
Tsuboguchi Hiroshi  vs.  Wataya Arata

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.460
I'm playing Wataya-kun again?

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.270
No! Please, no!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.270
Barely won last year

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.680
It's been a long time, Murao-kun.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.270
Murao Shinichi  vs.  Harada Hideo

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.270
It's good to see you again, Dr. Harada.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.610
<i>The Nagumo Society versus 
the Shiranami Society.</i>

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:37.400
<i>This is a prelude to
the Master tournament qualifiers.</i>

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.750
<i>Murao-kun, Arata-kun,
beat them into submission!</i>

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.080
Who are Ayase and Mashima playing?

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.970
Mashima's up against Sudo-san?!

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.920
Mashima Taichi  vs.  Sudo Akihito

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.320
Oh, you're still in it?

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.840
Lucky me.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.710
<i>That means Ayase's playing...</i>

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.100
Ayase Chihaya vs. Inokuma Haruka

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:08.150
Chihaya-chan's next opponent is a mother?

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.220
With two kids, no less.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.740
You think she's good?

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.090
Ayase!

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.670
Keep calm!

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:19.540
When you get to the quarterfinals,
 anyone you play is gonna be tough!

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.700
Just stay calm and play your own way!

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.990
Don't think of her as a former Queen
with four straight wins!

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.830
Former Queen?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.340
Wow, really?

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.700
<i>"Really"?</i>

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.930
<i>It's frightening that she didn't know!</i>

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.140
Yumin, don't miss this.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.580
Inokuma-san is sure to be 
in the Queen qualifiers.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.010
I don't want to be matched against her.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.180
No kidding, fool! Nobody does!

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.330
H-How good is she, exactly?

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.150
I've only seen her in videos myself,

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.450
but her game plan is highly unique.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:58.960
She's kinda like Wakamiya Shinobu, 
but with better game sense.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.770
What? <i>Better</i> game sense?!

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:03.600
<i>Can I make it through a match with Sudo-san?</i>

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.280
<i>Once he's sure his opponent ranks below him,</i>

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.890
<i>he arranges his cards in ways 
that seem to tease them</i>

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.370
<i>and uses his words to mess with them.</i>

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:16.570
<i>I need to keep it together.
This is my chance to make the semis.</i>

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.310
<i>Keep it together...</i>

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:23.520
Feels like a team match, doesn't it?

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.920
Four Shiranami Society players 
made it to the quarterfinals.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.990
That's a first!

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.770
This is a four-on-four 
team match in every way!

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.520
And of course, our goal is...

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:40.310
four wins for the Shiranami Society!

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.750
<i>That Harada still has no class whatsoever.</i>

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.020
<i>He made sure everyone would
hear him say that.</i>

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:51.780
<i>Dr. Harada is trying to give the impression
that the Shiranami Society has the momentum.</i>

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.590
<i>This is no big deal.</i>

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:58.030
Arata, let's both win two more matches 
and meet in the final.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.120
<i>The Nagumo Society has just as much momentum!</i>

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.940
<i>They're all a bunch of fools!</i>

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.380
<i>Both the Nagumo Society and 
the Shiranami Society!</i>

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.920
<i>The real battle is the Master and Queen 
tournament qualifiers in two weeks.</i>

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.150
Keep your eyes peeled, Yumin.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.350
Where'd Yusei go?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.000
<i>The Suihoku Society's watching closely to 
learn every last detail about the opposition.</i>

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.920
<i>We're the smartest ones here.</i>

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.210
<i>The one to watch is definitely 
Inokuma, grade 6.</i>

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.110
<i>Has she returned to her former self,
the one who was Queen?</i>

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:32.340
<i>If she has, there's no scarier opponent.</i>

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.840
<i>Is she going to make a full comeback?</i>

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.380
<i>A noteworthy high school player 
will be a good test for her.</i>

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.800
<i>Hang in there!</i>

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.270
<i>A team match with the 
Shiranami Society, huh?</i>

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.260
We'll be outside.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.610
<i>The reader is a member of
the Hiroshima Karuta Association,</i>

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.020
<i>full-time reader Hirota Koichiro, grade 6.</i>

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:03.850
<i>What a treat!</i>

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.740
Two minutes of memorization time remaining.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.240
<i>Chihaya-chan's playing Inokuma-san...</i>

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.360
<i>How far will she make it?</i>

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.510
<i>There's not much she'll learn from this,
but she will gain rare, valuable experience.</i>

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.170
<i>Even with Chihaya playing 
right next to me...</i>

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:26.370
Is "Impassionate" your best card, too?

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:29.610
I should probably move it, then.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.190
Over here? No, maybe over here...

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:35.180
<i>I'm preoccupied enough with my own match!</i>

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.090
<i>Oops.</i>

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:38.460
<i>Can't get distracted.</i>

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.680
<i>I need to focus on the lion in front of me!</i>

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.970
<i>Right. I'm not the club president today.</i>

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:48.010
We will now begin.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.760
Thank you for the game.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.730
Thank you for the game.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:06:02.860
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:12.110
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:14.980
<i>Preoccupied is fine. I just have to do this.</i>

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:23.350
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:28.960
<i>Look for the sound of the cuckoo</i>

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:36.730
<i>In the sleepy spring sunlight,</i>

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.330
<i>She got two in a row?</i>

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.470
<i>She's not just taking cards with speed alone,
unlike so many youngsters!</i>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.540
<i>She's being careful,</i>

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.380
<i>and her movements are sharp.</i>

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:47.090
I think I listen for whether 
the sound is high or low.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.140
<i>The pitch...</i>

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:52.550
<i>High...</i>

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:53.950
<i>Low...</i>

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.410
<i>High...</i>

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:56.660
<i>Low...</i>

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.020
<i>High...</i>

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.300
<i>Low...</i>

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:06.390
<i>A house left to the weeds 
welcomes no visitors</i>

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:07.650
<i>Maybe what we'll be seeing today 
isn't Inokuma Haruka's comeback,</i>

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.270
<i>but a new generation's takeover!</i>

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.830
<i>The sight of the lonely moon...</i>

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.220
<i>A fault...</i>

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.110
<i>That's a full-time reader for you.</i>

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:20.110
<i>The differences in pitch are so subtle.</i>

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.220
<i>Feel sorrow wash...</i>

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:24.920
<i>Though I prayed...</i>

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.240
<i>Inokuma-san got her back!</i>

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:34.470
<i>My fear is that you will forget 
your promise to never forget me,</i>

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.760
<i>The mood doesn't lie, 
irresponsible as it is.</i>

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.410
<i>It's filled with expectation for 
the bright shine of a new star.</i>

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:49.120
<i>It really takes passion 
to come back to the game.</i>

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:58.580
<i>so I would prefer to die now 
while I am still happy</i>

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.670
<i>The sky is the road home...</i>

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:05.650
<i>The fall wind parts...</i>

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.910
<i>It's hard to discern the pitch for "The" cards,</i>

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.830
<i>yet she could hear it?</i>

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.600
<i>A new star... who's in high school?</i>

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.370
<i>She's trying hard to discern the pitch,</i>

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.100
<i>but there's so much more to it.</i>

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:24.990
<i>There are many qualities to a sound.</i>

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.780
<i>High and low, strong and weak,</i>

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:33.250
<i>feminine and masculine, soft and sharp...</i>

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:37.330
<i>Whether the reader is from 
the east or the west...</i>

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:39.140
<i>clear and bright</i>

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:47.970
<i>After I determined to abandon 
my love, my only regret</i>

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.570
<i>She's fast!</i>

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:52.110
<i>Her ears... are picking it up now.</i>

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.200
<i>They're remembering what 
competitive karuta is.</i>

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:56.780
<i>Not only that...</i>

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.480
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.970
<i>Wha... What?!</i>

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:08.320
<i>Normally, as you take more cards,</i>

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.790
<i>you'd move your remaining 
cards toward the outside.</i>

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:15.800
<i>But she almost never rearranges her cards,</i>

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.660
<i>leaving them all over the place.</i>

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.980
<i>It's her unique play style.</i>

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.770
<i>You can't swipe whole rows to take a card.</i>

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.710
<i>It forces you to go for only 
the exact card you want.</i>

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:30.930
<i>Sakurazawa-san,</i>

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:34.820
<i>is this what you would call "passion"?</i>

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:38.320
<i>D-Dang, Inokuma-san is really good!</i>

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.440
<i>She's just as good as she was 
before her maternity leave!</i>

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.500
<i>I thought she'd already peaked...</i>

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.310
<i>And she was away
from the game so long, too...</i>

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.890
Daddy, where's Mommy?

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.440
Oh, Aki, you woke up?

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.180
Mommy's in the middle of a match.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:54.310
<i>It looks like...</i>

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.280
<i>She's actually looking to 
take back the Queen title?</i>

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.390
<i>I know I'm being greedy.</i>

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:05.790
Mommy! Where are you?!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.060
<i>But I want to show—</i>

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:16.420
<i>prove to one and all—</i>

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:19.510
<i>that I'm just coming into my prime!</i>

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:29.700
<i>That's him: the Nagumo Society's 
cleanup man, Murao-kun.</i>

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:32.570
<i>He didn't have much of a presence at first,</i>

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.690
<i>but his hours of practice, and the players 
he's practiced with, are paying off.</i>

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.860
<i>Dr. Harada's down by ten already...</i>

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.120
<i>He's a tough opponent.</i>

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:46.250
<i>These kids...</i>

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.470
<i>H-He's fast!</i>

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:57.460
<i>Not because his game sense is perfect, 
but because of his insane acceleration!</i>

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.210
<i>This is why I hate playing high schoolers.</i>

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:05.520
<i>He's improved even more since last year.</i>

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:09.980
<i>Lots of matches worth watching 
this time around...</i>

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.240
<i>I thought the young players' efforts 
would stand out above all.</i>

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.400
<i>But Inokuma's stealing the show!</i>

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.870
<i>I can't attack her side. 
Her defense is too solid.</i>

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:28.400
<i>Not only can she discern sounds 
accurately, but her card placement...</i>

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:31.310
<i>That's only advantageous 
for the one who always</i>

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:34.180
<i>puts all the cards in the same spots, 
and practices that way for years.</i>

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.880
<i>It's only advantageous for her.</i>

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:38.960
<i>Ayase...</i>

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:43.510
<i>Darn it! I want to watch President Mashima's
match too, but there's only one of me!</i>

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.390
<i>Hanano-san...</i>

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.200
<i>Mashima-senpai...</i>

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:58.010
<i>I still don't know much about 
the finer points of karuta,</i>

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.240
<i>but...</i>

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:02.530
Wait, did you really get that?

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:03.200
Huh?

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.750
Okay, then. If that's what you think.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:07.880
Keep it.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.570
Huh, so you couldn't see it...

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:14.080
<i>But...</i>

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:17.800
<i>Mashima-senpai's karuta has changed 
since the individual tournament</i>

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.590
<i>at the High School Championship.</i>

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.250
<i>Scary!</i>

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:26.020
<i>There's Sudo-kun's aggressive, 
offensive karuta! Good!</i>

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.190
Hey...

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:31.680
I'm not sure I'd believe it,

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.840
but are you in love with Ayase?

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.940
<i>He's hard to play against.</i>

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:48.150
<i>His karuta is so aggressive, it's scary...</i>

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:52.720
<i>But it's just an act. 
He's pushed to his limits, too.</i>

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:55.760
<i>That's what I'm gonna tell myself.</i>

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:58.680
<i>Mashima...</i>

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:00.390
<i>Relax.</i>

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:02.990
<i>Relax.</i>

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.420
<i>My opponent is strong, and that's why...</i>

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.660
<i>I have to test this.</i>

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.170
<i>I have to!</i>

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.310
<i>When winds blow oak leaves...</i>

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:15.930
<i>He's starting to cover
 the three-syllable cards.</i>

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:19.620
<i>And he's doing it by swinging through,
not just holding them down.</i>

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:24.280
<i>Mashima-kun was consciously trying to 
move quickly at the training camp, too.</i>

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.230
<i>He also practiced covering cards,
even those with few unique syllables.</i>

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.410
<i>That's Emuro-kun's specialty.</i>

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:32.870
<i>Test it...</i>

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:36.640
<i>Test what I've practiced,</i>

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.860
<i>and test myself.</i>

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:45.130
<i>Now this is interesting!</i>

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.220
Harada 19 - 10 Murao

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:54.480
Wataya 12 - 17 Tsuboguchi

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:58.230
Sudo 12 - 17 Mashima

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.400
Ayase 16 - 13 Inokuma

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:04.280
<i>All four of the Shiranami 
players are at a disadvantage.</i>

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.040
<i>It was all going too well.</i>

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:08.140
<i>Are they going to keep slipping?</i>

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:09.660
<i>Amazing...</i>

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:13.170
<i>It's amazing, Yama-chan.</i>

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.670
<i>There's far more depth 
to the world of sound!</i>

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.240
<i>Impassioned was your...</i>

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:21.620
<i>She took—</i>

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.620
Got there in time!

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.820
<i>"Got there in time"? What kind 
of thing is that to yell out?!</i>

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.880
<i>He has the worst etiquette of anyone here!</i>

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.020
<i>That's Dr. Harada's typical 
style of intimidation.</i>

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.650
<i>Will it work on Murao-san?</i>

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:48.410
<i>Dr. Harada's "Got there in time"...</i>

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.840
<i>He targeted his opponent's 
"Impassioned vows"</i>

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.670
<i>and got back to his own 
"Impassioned was" in time!</i>

00:14:56.630 --> 00:14:57.980
<i>Attack.</i>

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.520
<i>Attack!</i>

